now i know that this is going to  disappoint a lot of you guys but based  on some leaks  rumors and things that apple have said  themselves i am now confident that a  very powerful  intel base mac is coming later this year  so prepare to be surprised because this  is gonna get  interesting let's begin with some very  old leaks  that didn't really make much sense until  right now now i don't know if you  remember this but  over a year ago twitter user row game  discovered some very interesting bits of  code  within mac os beta pointing to brand new  navi 21 graphics card support coming to  the mac  and then in june right after apple  announced mac os big sur  at their wwdc event even more code was  discovered  pointing to newer navi 31 graphics  support  also coming to the mac so you might be  thinking that all of that was meant for  the 27-inch  intel-based imac that we got released in  august  but the very best graphics card option  in that imac  is the 5700xt which is actually based  on navi 10 not 21 and certainly not  31. this basically shows that apple was  planning on adding support for those  newer architectures in the future  which might seem a little bit weird  unless they're planning on releasing  another intel-based mac before the  transition  to apple silicon is completed and i  believe that's exactly what apple is  going to be doing  mostly because of this quote from last  year's wwc  event we plan to continue to support and  release new versions of mac os for intel  based macs for years to come  in fact we have some new intel based  macs in the pipeline  that we're really excited about yes tim  cook mentioned  some intel based macs and as we all know  the only one they've released so far is  the 27-inch imac  which shows that they've got at least  one more intel based mac coming in the  future and as of right now  after seeing how incredibly good apple's  very first  and weakest m1 ship has been performing  compared to intel chips  like the slaughterfest that happened in  one of our latest laptop comparisons  everybody already knows that they should  avoid intel  on the consumer level max because apple  silicon  is just too good however there is still  one mac that could potentially fit the  bill  for getting an intel based chip and that  is of course  the mac pro so let me explain why the  current 2019 mac pro is now the only mac  that's available with an intel xeon  champ and that chip is extremely  important for specific workflows like  high-end  mathematical and scientific computation  since xeon chips are fine-tuned to run  complex tasks with very wide bit depths  and of course the ecc ram is very  desirable  for those workflows as well and it's  exclusive  to high-end machines like the mac pro on  top of that  it supports up to 1.5 terabytes of ram  which is absolutely overkill for 99 of  the people out  there but there are very specific  workflows  that can actually utilize all of it and  there are huge corporations  that will pay thousands upon thousands  of dollars  for a machine like the mac pro and if  you really think about it it would be a  shame  if apple spent years on research and  development as well as  tons of resources on all of the custom  tooling  and custom components in the 2019 mac  pro  just to completely ditch all of that  when the new apple silicon mac pro is  released  and we know for sure that the new apple  silicon mac pro is not going to be using  the same cheese grater chassis because  it's overkill  with the huge motherboard and everything  else and by simply looking at the new  24-inch imac  we know that apple wants to go smaller  with their new apple silicon max  so what i'm trying to say is that it  totally makes sense for apple  to reuse the current mac pro's design  for  at least one more intel based mac pro  refresh  and we've actually got quite a few leaks  and rumors to support this conclusion  a couple of months back mark german from  bloomberg a very reliable apple analyst  claimed that apple was working on two  mac pro  high-end desktop machines he even  mentioned that one of them will be a  refreshed model  that will reuse the same chassis and  that will continue to use  intel processors which is what this  video is all  about and of course there will be a  second version  that will use apple's own chips and be  less than half the size of the current  mac pro  so based on that and everything else  that i've already mentioned  the intel based mac pro is definitely  happening  and here's why i think it's gonna get  released this december  first off apple's super high-end  machines like the 2013 mac pro  the 2017 imac pro and the 2019 mac pro  were always released in december because  it's targeted towards huge businesses  who need to get tax write-offs before  the end of the year  by investing their extra profits and the  reason i think that it's coming this  december and not  next year is because i believe that's  when the apple silicon mac pro is gonna  get released  right at the end of their two-year  timeline for the transition  but the even more telling reason is  because of this massive leak  that recently showed up an apple mac pro  exclusive  amd radeon pro w6900x gpu  has randomly popped up on geekbench with  the highest metal score  ever seen on any mac in this test even  beating out the regular  6900 xt which this x card is based on  now there are some people that say that  this is a fake result  that's actually using a hackintosh  system because  it's noted as using an intel core  processor  but i actually think that it's legit and  here's why  that i9 core chip is using intel's  latest cascade lake architecture  but since the latest xeons haven't yet  made it onto store shelves  i think that geekbench didn't recognize  the new xeon chip  so it defaulted to that 12 core chip  that it does recognize  and on top of that if it actually was a  hackintosh with a regular 6900 xt  graphics card  how would it be able to get a score  that's quite a bit higher  the test result clearly shows a w6900x  which can only happen if support for  that card is already built into macos  which we saw with those previous leaks  within mac os beta code  and the wx cards use apple's custom mpx  slot  which can't be put into a hackintosh so  this is likely a legit  leaked benchmark result and just a  couple of weeks ago  support for this new navi 21 generation  of amd gpus  was finally added to mac os showing that  apple is working on the software  for these new cards and likely for this  brand new  w6900x for the mac pro and if you're  wondering how it's able to get a higher  score  than the other 6900 xt it's likely  because it'll be coming  with 32 gigabytes of vram instead of the  regular cards  16 and we know this because apple's  w5700  xt in the mac pro has 16 gigs of vram  compared to only eight on every other  5700 xd card on the market  and going even further i have two very  good reasons for why  this new intel based mac pro is gonna  get released  this december first off amd's new 6000  series desktop gpus  like the 6900xt are already on the  market  so if apple waited even longer to  release a mac pro  with the w6900x it wouldn't feel as  fresh  or powerful anymore and second intel  finally launched their new 3rd gen xeons  last month  based on the new 10 nanometer ice lake  architecture  which should give it some pretty good  advantages that apple would definitely  want  in their refresh mac pro but this  creates a huge  problem these new xeon chips require a  brand  new socket which also requires a brand  new  motherboard this means that apple can't  simply refresh the same listing page  for the current mac pro and add those  new intel chips  they literally have to redesign the  motherboard to add  the new socket which means that it needs  to have a new part number  which in turn means that it's likely  going to be named the 2021  mac pro so yeah if you take all of the  information  from this video everything points to  apple releasing a new  intel based mac pro this december based  on  the current cheese grater chassis so  there you guys go  that was all of my reasoning for why  we're getting a new intel based mac pro  this year  and if you totally disagree with me  comment your thoughts  down below but if you enjoyed it click  that circle above to subscribe  check out one of those two videos right  there thanks for watching and we'll see  you  in the next video  [Music]

